#: manual/tutorial/float_backend.md:94
msgid "$i^i = e^{i \\cdot i\\pi/2} = e^{-\\pi/2}$ is real. Integer exponents use exact binary powering, so $i^2$ is exactly $-1$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/float_backend.md:97
msgid "Do not take non-integer powers of negative real numbers yet. `arg` returns $2\\pi$ instead of $\\pi$ on the negative real axis, so the angle of the result is wrong:"
